{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791029562,"nonce":"prrMT9qrp9WqXP2QiYiTooaGbDs=","title":"Support full SVG instead of rejecting features","message":"SvgParser threw for anything outside its typed model: gradients and patterns (url() paints), nested \u003csvg\u003e, \u003ctext\u003e, \u003cuse\u003e, \u003clinearGradient\u003e, filters, unknown colour names, units other than px, unknown transform functions and keyword values. ashui should draw any SVG.\n\nAs done:\n- The rasterizer (usvg/resvg through blinc_svg) gets the original document, written back canonically from Haxe's Xml (sorted attributes, no comments, SVG and XLink namespaces declared), not ashui's model re-serialised.\n- SvgParser stays as a typed model and compile-time check. Elements outside it are OtherElement nodes, paints it cannot read are Other paints; lengths convert absolute units; unreadable values are left to the renderer.\n- Errors remain only for malformed input: not XML, a root that is not \u003csvg\u003e, path data that does not parse.\n- A mask (rasterised white, tinted when drawn) only when every paint is currentColor and there are no elements outside the model; everything else is rasterised with the element's colour as the root's `color`, unless the root sets its own.\n- hxx passes text content inside \u003csvg\u003e through, for \u003ctext\u003e and \u003cstyle\u003e.\n- blinc_svg's svg_raster_images feature on, for JPEG, GIF and WebP \u003cimage\u003e; the release hdll grows from about 3.1 MB to 3.4 MB.","files":null}]}